veritas (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * maak agents writes AGENTS.md from the two skills pinned in maak.scm and
    the practices kept in the same file.  Each skill is imported whole and the
    practices name no project path, module or task, so the task is the recipe
    for another repository.
  * The recipes, the container image metadata and the package homepages name
    github.com/jjba23/veritas now that Codeberg is archived.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

veritas (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * veritas is MIT licensed: LICENSE replaces COPYING, and the packaging, the
    container image labels and the manual page name the new licence.
  * CI/CD runs on GitHub Actions (Byggsteg), replacing the Woodpecker pipeline.
  * The rerun tests build their fixtures with the positional constructor, which
    Guile 3.0.10's keyword-call inlining broke; make-raw-pre-test-result is
    exported.
  * The guide documents rerunning only the tests that failed, the record every
    run writes, and the full environment table.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

veritas (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the coverage suite: loading its compiled fixture no longer leaves the
    loader in the fixture's module, so the file's suites are evaluated where
    `suite' is defined.
  * Flaky tests get a reporter level of their own (`flaky`), and the GitHub
    step summary gains a flaky column.
  * Change-aware selection reads the data files a test names, not only the
    modules it imports.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

veritas (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Change-aware runs: --changed/--since select the test files a diff reaches
    through #:use-module imports, and --list prints that selection without
    running it.
  * #:retries, veritas-retries and VERITAS_RETRIES rerun a failing test; a test
    that then passes is counted as flaky and marked flaky="true" in the JUnit
    document.
  * --trace records suites, tests and assertions step by step, and --show-trace
    prints the timeline of the last run.
  * (veritas all) re-exports the whole framework behind one import.
  * docs/incremental.org, docs/debugging.org and docs/batteries.org.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

veritas (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Assertions defer work with (lazy expr) instead of the quoted (comp ...)
    forms, which lost lexical scope and compiled at run time.
  * Test results carry the file they were declared in, written into the JUnit
    document and used by CI annotations; lines are opt-in.
  * The wall clock and the running test's location are injectable parameters,
    and report ordering is deterministic.
  * Assertion execution is about 11% faster; report generation no longer scans
    the case list once per class.
  * The README is a landing page; the guide lives in docs/.

 -- Josep Bigorra <jjbigorra@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

veritas (0.11.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Test results record their file and duration: the JUnit document carries
    file, suite path and time per test, and adds a GitHub Actions reporter that
    writes check annotations and a step summary.

